course: dictionary
lesson: 4486
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The word hatch is one of them. To find the right meaning, read the words around it: they are its context. «The chick cracks the shell to hatch.» Here the words shell and chick tell you hatch means coming out of an egg.
explain: The same word can mean something very different in another sentence. «Ben climbed through the hatch into the loft.» There is no egg here. A hatch is a small door or opening, and the loft is the clue. Always ask: which meaning fits this sentence?
explain: Try your meaning in the sentence and see if it still makes sense. «Mia and Sam hatch a plan in the playground.» Swap in make a secret plan: Mia and Sam make a secret plan in the playground. It fits, so that is the meaning.
fact: Hatch can be a verb or a noun. As a verb it is something you do, and as a noun it is a thing.
fact: To hatch means for a baby bird, reptile or fish to break out of its egg.
fact: To hatch a plan means to make a secret plan.
fact: A hatch is a small door or opening in a floor, wall, ship or plane.
fact: «Don't count your chickens before they've hatched» means do not expect good results before they happen.
exercise: «Some rare birds lay a second egg, so a zoo can hatch two chicks instead of one.» What does hatch mean here? | *Come out of an egg | Close a window tightly | Make a secret plan | Lift up a small door in a floor
exercise: Mum says, «Let's hatch a plan for Saturday.» What does hatch mean? | To shut a window | To cook a big meal | *To make a secret plan | To count the chickens
exercise: Ben climbed through the hatch into the loft. What is a hatch? | *A small door or opening | A bird that lives by the sea | A kind of egg shell | A plan made in secret
test: «In spring toads walk back to the pond where they hatched.» What does hatched mean here? | *Came out of their eggs | Walked across the road | Opened a small door | Made a secret plan
test: Ruby says a hatch in a ship is a kind of bird. What is a hatch? | *A small door or opening in a floor, wall, ship or plane | A bird that lives near the sea | A plan made in secret | A kind of egg
exam: Which sentence uses hatch to mean a baby comes out of its egg? | *A chicken egg takes about 21 days to hatch if kept warm | The workers opened the hatch in the ship's deck | Climb through the escape hatch if the door is blocked | Ella and Tom hatch a plan to surprise Dad
